# Naming check disabled for this directory only.
#
# mps_reader.cpp and solu_reader.cpp are vendored from spoorendonk/mipx and
# carry a "port the diff here and bump the last synced commit" contract in
# their headers. Upstream spells its helpers camelBack (`parseReal`,
# `isSection`, `parseSection`), so renaming them to this project's lower_case
# would put a permanent, purely cosmetic delta between the two trees and make
# the next sync harder to review -- against the Reference Correctness rule in
# CLAUDE.md. Four findings, all in mps_reader.cpp (solu_reader.cpp has none).
#
# Everything else in the root .clang-tidy still applies here; only the naming
# check is off. The tradeoff is that the three native adapters in this
# directory (mps_to_model.cpp, nl_to_model.cpp, nl_reader.cpp) also lose naming
# coverage -- they are clean today, so keep an eye on new code here.
---
# InheritParentConfig is load-bearing. Without it clang-tidy REPLACES the root
# `Checks:` with this one rather than appending to it, leaving only the
# always-on `clang-diagnostic-*` -- `clang-tidy -p build src/io/mps_to_model.cpp`
# then exits 1 with "Error: no checks enabled." and all five translation units
# here go unlinted. Verify any edit with
# `cd src/io && ../../.venv/bin/clang-tidy --dump-config` -- the pinned copy,
# because a system clang-tidy of another vintage merges a different default set
# -- and check the root's check list is actually present in the output.
#
# The exemption below is LIVE: issue #121 cleared readability-identifier-naming
# from the root ratchet, so the check now runs everywhere except here. Deleting
# this file, or the line below, turns the four vendored mps_reader.cpp findings
# back into push-blocking warnings. Confirm it still bites after any edit with
# the --dump-config command above: the root's check list must be present AND
# followed by -readability-identifier-naming.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-identifier-naming
